{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788969884,"nonce":"Zfy1dKcPVkQXm+vs0vmQcDA9GaM=","title":"use-item verb: CompUsable items are unreachable (skilltrainers, techprof core, mech serums)","message":"Every `CompProperties_Usable` item in the game is dead weight to the agent: it can be bought and hauled, and never used.\n\nFound while planning openrun-20260909, whose brief asks for skilltrainers and fast-tracked research. Both are in Dad's catalog and both are unusable.\n\n## What is out of reach\n\n- `Neurotrainer_*` — all 12 skilltrainers, 750 each in the catalog, `CompUseEffect_LearnSkill`.\n- `TechprofSubpersonaCore` — 1000, `CompUseEffect_FinishResearchProject`. **Instantly completes the current research project.** This is the single largest research lever in the game.\n- `MechSerumHealer`, `MechSerumResurrector`, psytrainers — same comp.\n\n## Why `consume` does not cover it\n\n`PawnOrderVerbs.Consume` gates on `thing.def.ingestible == null || !thing.def.ingestible.showIngestFloatOption` -\u003e `not-ingestible`, then issues `JobDefOf.Ingest`. Verified against the shipped defs: `TechprofSubpersonaCore` and `MechSerumHealer` in `Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Exotic.xml` have no `\u003cingestible\u003e` block and carry `CompProperties_Usable` + `CompProperties_UseEffect` + `CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf`. The right job is `JobDefOf.UseItem`, not `Ingest`.\n\n## The gate to reproduce\n\nThe player's route is `CompUsable.CompFloatMenuOptions` -\u003e `CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy(pawn, out string failReason)` -\u003e `TryStartUseJob`. `CanBeUsedBy` is the widget's own precondition and must be cited and re-implemented, not bypassed; `CompUseEffect.CanBeUsedBy` on each effect comp is the second half (e.g. `CompUseEffect_LearnSkill` refuses a pawn whose skill is already maxed or whose passion/incapability blocks it).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `use {pawn, thing}` exists, reproduces `CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` and every `CompUseEffect.CanBeUsedBy` on the target, and cites both by file and member in its refusal.\n- A pawn ordered to use a `Neurotrainer_Shooting` gains the skill levels; the item is destroyed.\n- A pawn ordered to use a `TechprofSubpersonaCore` finishes the current research project; `research` shows it complete and `current: null` afterwards.\n- Refusal cases answer `ok:false` with a gate name, not an exception: no current research project for the core, maxed skill for a trainer, unreachable item, pawn incapable.\n- An item with no `CompUsable` answers `not-usable` and names `consume` when the def is ingestible instead.\n- `queue` is honoured the way `consume` honours it.","files":null}]}